From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TheDBP <TheDBP@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 18:04:49 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] ether: ImsBridge -- bind the 7.1 ims.apk to the modern
 telephony stack

ims.apk implements com.android.ims.internal.IImsService, the pre-P IMS binding Android 9 deleted.
frameworks/opt/telephony still carries the compat path (ImsServiceControllerCompat,
MmTelFeatureCompatAdapter) behind android.telephony.ims.compat.ImsService, so the gap is one
translation layer, not a rewrite.

The legacy interfaces are hand-written AIDL in org.codeaurora.ims.legacy, matching the rename
already applied to the rebuilt apk. Method ORDER is transcribed from the 7.1 binary's TRANSACTION_*
constants, because AIDL numbers transactions by declaration order and the far end is stock's
compiled 2016 code that cannot be recompiled to agree with us. Verified after building: the
generated stub numbers open=1 through getMultiEndpointInterface=16, matching 7.1, and advertises
the same renamed descriptor the apk does.

The shape difference the bridge absorbs is that 7.1 is serviceId-keyed -- open() returns an int
every later call carries -- while a MMTelFeature instance already implies a session, so the bridge
holds the id.

Working: startSession/endSession, isConnected, isOpened, addRegistrationListener, createCallProfile,
turnOnIms, turnOffIms, setUiTTYMode, and the registration-listener adapter (ten callbacks map
directly; registrationFeatureCapabilityChanged has no 13 equivalent and is dropped explicitly).
Parcelable conversion is done for ImsCallProfile, ImsReasonInfo and ImsStreamMediaProfile -- each is
a handful of instance fields, not the dozens the constant lists suggest.

The six methods that return or take a 7.1 sub-interface throw UnsupportedOperationException for now
rather than returning null, which would defer the failure somewhere unrelated. They need a wrapper
apiece and their .aidl filled in with real method order first.
